`opentelemetry-sdk`: (fork-only, not upstream) `Span.record_exception` attaches the source code of every frame in the exception's traceback to the `exception` event, as an `exception.stack_details` JSON array (each entry: `exception.file`, `exception.line`, `exception.function_name`, `exception.function_body`, `exception.start_line`, `exception.end_line`, `exception.is_file_external`), plus `exception.language`. Large functions are windowed to 10 lines above/below the failing line. On by default; opt out with `MW_RECORD_EXCEPTION_SOURCE=false`. Cap the serialized size with `MW_RECORD_EXCEPTION_SOURCE_MAX_CHARS` (default 8192).
